Title: Rain Check
Credit: Written by
Author: J. Writer

INT. DINER - NIGHT

A near-empty diner. Neon buzzes in the window. MARA (30s) wipes the counter without looking at it.

MARA
(not looking up)
We close in ten minutes.

TOM (O.S.)
Then I will be quick.

The door chimes. TOM (40s), soaked to the bone, drops a small box on the counter.

MARA
That is not a coffee order.

TOM
It is not.

EXT. PARKING LOT - CONTINUOUS

Rain hammers the roofs of three parked cars. A truck idles with its lights off.

TOM (V.O.)
I should have called first.

CUT TO:

INT. DINER - LATER

Mara opens the box. She goes very still.

MARA
Where did you find this?

TOM
Where you left it.

FADE OUT.
